class.description:
The get variable node has no flow ports and one data output, [code]value[/code] (any type). It reads the variable [member FlowVariableNode.variable_name] from the blackboard when another node reads its [code]value[/code].
Its runtime behavior comes with the playback, which is a later feature; until then the node only has its properties and ports.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
var get_gold := FlowGetVariableNode.new()
get_gold.variable_name = &"gold"
var get_id := graph.add_node(get_gold)
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
var getGold = new FlowGetVariableNode { VariableName = "gold" };
int getId = graph.AddNode(getGold);
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
